<title>SOUTH KOREA: Hanil Cement sets 1-for-10 bonus issue.</title>
<headline>Hanil Cement sets 1-for-10 bonus issue.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Hanil Cement Manufacturing Co Ltd has set a 1-for-10 bonus issue in March, a company statement said.</p>
<p>The statement said Hanil would issue 449,308 new common shares for shareholders as of March 15.</p>
<p>The bonus issue would boost the company's paid-in capital to 25.11 billion won from the current 22.87 billion, it said.</p>
<p>Hanil shares closed at 43,700 won on Wednesday, down 700.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5643</p>
</text>
